1. Identify all orders within the specified date range ('Summer Beverages 1997'). This involves filtering by OrderDate in that year and assuming summer months (typically June, July, August) are included.
2. Join the 'Orders' table with the "Order Details" to get UnitPrice for each order item sold during this period.
3. Filter orders based on Products.CategoryID linked to Beverages category from Categories table.
4. Sum up all revenue by multiplying UnitPrice and Quantity, then summing these amounts across filtered rows. This will give us the total revenue for 'Beverages' during summer 1997.
5. Round this value off to two decimal places as requested.

