Response: ## reasoning ##:
To find the top customer by gross margin in 1997, we need to calculate the gross margin for each sale made that year. Gross Margin can be calculated using UnitPrice and Quantity from "Order Details" table along with an estimated CostOfGoods which is approximated as 70% of UnitPrice if not available directly. We will then sum these margins per customer within the specified year, sort them in descending order to find the top one, and return their CustomerID (as a string) alongside the corresponding gross margin value (as a float).

## sql_query ##:
```sql
WITH GrossMargins AS (
    SELECT 
        o.CustomerID,
        SUM((od.UnitPrice * od.Quantity) - (0.7 * od.UnitPrice * od.Quantity)) as margin
    FROM Orders o
    JOIN "Order Details" od ON o.OrderID = od.OrderID
    WHERE YEAR(o.OrderDate) = 1997
    GROUP BY o.CustomerID
)
SELECT 
    CustomerName, MAX(margin) as margin
FROM GrossMargins gm
JOIN Customers c ON gm.CustomerID = c.CustomerID
GROUP BY CustomerName
OR

